0..74 Comment "// A program decides an overt bounded existential through `std.reals.Eff`,"
75..131 Comment "// the host interface of exact reals. The existential is"
132..212 Comment "// `∃ x ∈ [1, 2] (3 < x · x)`. `gandr run exists.gandr` prints `holds`. The"
213..289 Comment "// same `decided` runs under a handler of this source, a second model of the"
290..303 Comment "// interface."
304..306 Comment "//"
307..383 Comment "// The domain of the plan is the closed interval `[1, 2]`. The domain states"
384..459 Comment "// its overtness at the reference 1 and its compactness at the reference 2."
460..538 Comment "// The existential names the overtness as its evidence, and the compactness as"
539..603 Comment "// the evidence of its dual. The host registers both references."
604..606 Comment "//"
607..684 Comment "// `decide` mints a machine on the two poles of the root. The pole that holds"
685..761 Comment "// searches the domain breadth first for a subinterval where the body holds."
762..837 Comment "// It certifies in 13 steps, and the checker replays its certificate before"
838..916 Comment "// the host replies `holds`. The pole that fails suspends after 10 steps, when"
917..991 Comment "// a step of its search concludes the other pole. So the machine spends 23"
992..1022 Comment "// quanta of its budget of 32."
1023..1025 Comment "//"
1026..1095 Comment "// - see: `corpus/model/reals/forall.gandr` — the compact universal"
1096..1170 Comment "// - see: `crates/theory-exact-reals/src/bisection.rs` — the search of a"
1171..1186 Comment "//   quantifier"
1188..1220 Comment "// The console\'s host interface."
